# App Flow Document

## User Journeys & Application Workflows

This document outlines the key user journeys and application workflows for the Stock Management SaaS platform.

## Authentication Flow

### Sign Up Process
1. Organization admin visits landing page
2. Admin selects "Sign Up" and enters organization details:
   - Organization name
   - Admin email
   - Password
   - Select subscription plan
3. System creates new organization with tenant ID
4. Admin receives welcome email with verification link
5. First login prompts for additional organization details

### Login Process
1. User visits login page
2. Enters email and password
3. System validates credentials against tenant database
4. If valid, generates JWT with user permissions and tenant ID
5. Redirects to dashboard
6. If invalid, shows error message

### Password Recovery
1. User clicks "Forgot Password"
2. Enters email address
3. System sends reset link if email exists
4. User sets new password via secure link

### User Invitation Flow
1. Organization admin invites user via email
2. System generates temporary access link
3. New user sets password and completes profile
4. System assigns predefined role

## Dashboard Flow

### Main Dashboard
1. User logs in and lands on dashboard
2. Dashboard displays:
   - Stock overview (low stock alerts, total products)
   - Recent sales summary
   - Sales trends (daily/weekly/monthly)
   - Top selling products
   - Pending actions (approvals, orders to fulfill)

### Analytics Dashboard
1. User navigates to analytics section
2. System presents filters for date range, product categories
3. Displays visualizations:
   - Sales performance charts
   - Inventory turnover rates
   - Revenue analysis
   - Profit margins

## Product Management Flow

### Adding New Products
1. User navigates to Products module
2. Selects "Add New Product"
3. Completes product form:
   - SKU, name, description
   - Category
   - Cost and selling price
   - Tax information
   - Initial stock level
   - Minimum stock threshold
4. Submits form
5. System validates input
6. Creates product in database
7. Initializes inventory record

### Bulk Product Import
1. User selects "Import Products"
2. Downloads template spreadsheet
3. Fills in product data
4. Uploads completed spreadsheet
5. System validates data
6. Displays validation results with errors
7. User confirms import
8. System creates products and inventory records

### Editing Products
1. User finds product via search or browse
2. Selects product to edit
3. Modifies details
4. Saves changes
5. System updates product information
6. Logs change history

## Inventory Management Flow

### Stock Adjustment
1. User navigates to Inventory module
2. Selects product for adjustment
3. Enters new quantity or adjustment amount
4. Provides reason for adjustment
5. Submits change
6. System updates inventory
7. Creates stock movement record

### Stock Replenishment
1. User identifies low stock items
2. Selects "Replenish Stock"
3. Either:
   - Enters quantities manually
   - Uploads spreadsheet with replenishment data
4. Reviews and confirms
5. System updates inventory levels
6. Creates stock movement records

### Low Stock Alerts
1. System runs scheduled job to check inventory levels
2. Identifies products below minimum threshold
3. Generates alerts in dashboard
4. Sends email notification to designated users

## Sales Process Flow

### Creating a Sale
1. User navigates to Sales module
2. Selects "New Sale"
3. Searches for and selects client (or creates new)
4. Adds products to sale:
   - Searches product catalog
   - Selects product
   - Enters quantity
   - System calculates price with taxes
5. Adjusts discounts if needed
6. Reviews sale details
7. Finalizes sale
8. System:
   - Creates sale record
   - Reduces inventory quantities
   - Creates stock movement records
   - Updates sales statistics

### Sale Returns Process
1. User locates original sale
2. Selects "Process Return"
3. Selects items being returned and quantities
4. Indicates reason for return
5. Processes return
6. System:
   - Creates return record
   - Adjusts inventory levels
   - Updates sales statistics

## Client Management Flow

### Adding New Clients
1. User navigates to Clients module
2. Selects "Add New Client"
3. Enters client details:
   - Name/Company
   - Contact information
   - Address
   - Payment terms
4. Saves client record

### Client History View
1. User searches for client
2. Views client profile
3. Accesses tabs for:
   - Purchase history
   - Outstanding balances
   - Contact information
   - Notes/comments

## Organization Management Flow

### User Management
1. Admin navigates to Organization module
2. Selects "Users" section
3. Views existing users
4. Can add new users:
   - Enter email and name
   - Assign role/permissions
   - Send invitation
5. Can edit existing users:
   - Change role
   - Activate/deactivate account

### Role & Permission Management
1. Admin navigates to "Roles & Permissions"
2. Views existing roles
3. Can create new roles:
   - Name role
   - Select permissions
   - Set description
4. Can edit existing roles:
   - Add/remove permissions
   - Rename
   - Set as default for new users

### Subscription & Billing
1. Admin navigates to "Subscription"
2. Views current plan details
3. Can upgrade/downgrade plan
4. Access billing history
5. Update payment method

## Report Generation Flow

### Standard Reports
1. User navigates to Reports module
2. Selects report type:
   - Sales summary
   - Inventory valuation
   - Product performance
   - Client purchase history
3. Sets parameters (date range, categories, etc.)
4. Generates report
5. Views on-screen or exports (PDF, Excel)

### Custom Reports
1. User selects "Custom Report"
2. Selects data fields to include
3. Sets filters and grouping options
4. Previews report
5. Saves report configuration for future use
6. Exports if needed

## Data Export/Import Flow

### Data Export
1. User navigates to relevant module
2. Selects "Export Data"
3. Chooses format (CSV, Excel)
4. Sets filters if needed
5. Initiates export
6. Downloads file

### Data Import
1. User selects "Import Data"
2. Chooses data type (products, clients, etc.)
3. Downloads template
4. Fills template with data
5. Uploads completed file
6. System validates data
7. Shows preview with validation results
8. User confirms import
9. System processes data and creates records

## System Notifications Flow

### Alert Types
- Low stock notifications
- New user invitations
- Completed imports/exports
- System updates

### Notification Delivery
1. System generates notification
2. Stores in notification center
3. Displays count in UI header
4. Delivers via selected channels:
   - In-app notification
   - Email
   - Dashboard alerts

## Error Handling Flow

### Validation Errors
1. User submits form with invalid data
2. System validates input
3. Displays specific error messages next to fields
4. Preserves valid input data
5. User corrects errors and resubmits

### System Errors
1. Application encounters error
2. Logs detailed error for debugging
3. Shows user-friendly message
4. Provides recovery options where possible

## Mobile-Specific Flows

### Mobile Inventory Check
1. User logs in via mobile device
2. Scans product barcode
3. Views current inventory level
4. Can adjust quantities directly

### Mobile Sales Entry
1. User creates new sale on mobile
2. Scans products or selects from list
3. Completes sale with simplified flow
4. Syncs with central database